[Unit]
Description=Slice for herdr terminal holders, outside systemd-oomd's reach
Documentation=man:systemd.resource-control(5) man:systemd-oomd.service(8)

[Slice]
# Omarchy marks app.slice ManagedOOMSwap/MemoryPressure=kill, and oomd kills a
# whole cgroup at once. herdr runs every pane in one hc-hold-*.service, so it is
# always the biggest candidate there and a kill took down every terminal.
# This slice sets no ManagedOOM*, so oomd never picks it; under real OOM the
# kernel kills a single process instead (the holder has OOMPolicy=continue).
